    summary=dict(raw=raw,conditions={},comparisons=pairs,examples=examples,scaling={k:{f:r[f] for f in ['wcsp','delta','wins','losses','ties']} for k,r in zip(['unscaled_v2','scaled_matched','scaled_calibrated'],scaling)})
    lines=['# PanNuke: cost scaling and biological sibling ablation','','## Scope and protocol','', '- Original block-fidelity V1/V2 experiment is preserved unchanged.', '- Scaling runs first; sibling ablation follows on original unscaled V1, with no block unaries. These are separate questions.', '- Exact original 100 comparison patches, full 256x256 TP probabilities/GT, six levels, 12 development patches, five-class pooled mIoU and paired 5,000-patch bootstrap.', '- Four comparison IDs (908, 2216, 2330, 2354) overlap upstream beta-development data discovered after the original run. Follow-up uses previously inspected data and is exploratory, not a fresh confirmation.', '- Reflect padding approximates border context. Patient/slide independence and checkpoint training exposure remain unknown.', '', '## 1. BCSS-style scaling','', '| Term | Original | Scaled |','|---|---|---|','| Block unary | gamma x -log(mean P) | original x block area |','| Sibling edge | sibling/4 x C_level | original x block side |','| Parent-child mismatch | parent x mismatch | original x child area |','', '- Six levels, scale-specific tables and four-connected graph stay fixed. This borrows cost scaling, not the complete BCSS pipeline.', '- Matched run: sibling=.3, parent=.1, gamma=.3, exactly as old V2; only scale factors change.', '- Calibrated run: parent chosen on original 12 development patches from .01/.03/.1/.3/.5; sibling=.3 and gamma=.3 fixed. Selected parent=.01 before comparison.', '', '| Method | Bio mIoU | Delta vs raw (pp) | W/L/T |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
