    for key,label in zip(KEYS,LABELS):lines.append(f'- {label}: {summary["conditions"][key]["seconds"]:.3f} seconds total across 100 patches.')
    lines+=['## Limits and future questions','', '- Same sibling multiplier across scales; distinct learned tables share the fixed biological reference prior, which may not mean the same thing at each scale.', '- Dead fitting data: two patches; no dominant Dead 32x32 fitting blocks. Sparse coarse-scale relations are smoothed rather than empirically established.', '- Simple mismatch parent-child cost; blocks mix nuclei with abundant Background; coarse labels are soft dominant states.', '- Local minima do not establish global optima or biological validity. Higher-level label changes alone do not establish causal contribution.', '- Next: check whether background-dominant block summaries or class-specific parent-child costs protect rare nuclei; validate any chosen redesign on genuinely new patches. Do not tune on these outcomes.', '', '## Reproduction','', '```bash','python -m unittest discover -s experiments/pannuke_wcsp/scaling_siblings_20261109 -p "test_*.py" -v','python experiments/pannuke_wcsp/scaling_siblings_20261109/run.py','python experiments/pannuke_wcsp/scaling_siblings_20261109/report.py','```','', '- Existing outputs refuse overwrite. Inputs reference the preserved hierarchy_20261109/cache. protocol.json and scaling_frozen.json record selection before comparison.', '- Tables, per-patch labels, level labels, confusion arrays, CSV/JSON, paired intervals and logs are retained.', '- Deliverable 6 edits are explicitly deferred until the 4:10 p.m. review. No commit or push is performed.','']
